  <para style="h">Hakai</para>
  <para style="toc1">Hakai</para>
  <para style="toc2">Hakai</para>
  <para style="toc3">Hak</para>
  <para style="mt1">Hakai</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="HAG 1" />
  <para style="s1">Ikood Adibọp Ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HAG 1:1" />Ke ayọhọ isua iba ke ukara Adidem Dariọs, ke akpa usen ke ayọhọ afiọñ itiokeed, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaato inua prọfed Hakai adisịm Serubabel ayịn Sieltiel, a-akedooho adaukara ke Yuda, ñko ye Yọsua ayịn Yosadak,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Ke usem Hibru </char><char style="fqa" closed="false">Yehosadak</char><char style="ft" closed="false">asʌk ado</char><char style="fq" closed="false">Yosadak; </char><char style="ft" closed="false">se ñko ke Hak 1:12 ye 14</char></note> a-akedooho akwa aku:<verse eid="HAG 1:1" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="HAG 1:2" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado mi: “Mbon ami ebo, ‘Ini ikemme adimaana mbọp ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.’ ”<verse eid="HAG 1:2" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="HAG 1:3" />Ndin ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaato prọfed Hakai adi: <verse eid="HAG 1:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HAG 1:4" />“Nte a-akem ini a-anaaha ndufo ke idem ndufo edʌñ ke mme ufọk atian, ke ini ufọk ami abaaha ke ñwuudo?”<verse eid="HAG 1:4" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="HAG 1:5" />Idahami se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado mi: “Nekke kọọk iwuod baña mme usʌñ mfo. <verse eid="HAG 1:5" /><verse number="6" style="v" sid="HAG 1:6" />Ndufo emaetọ uwak-uwak, ado edọk ntək-ntək. Ndufo emaedia ñkpọ, ado ikoppo uyʌkkọ. Ndufo emaenwọñ ukọd, ado ikoppo uyʌkkọ. Ndufo emaesịne afọñ, ado ikoppo ufiob ke idem. Ndufo emaebọ akʌkutom, ado e-edọñ ammọ ke asịtte adu ekpad.”<verse eid="HAG 1:6" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="HAG 1:7" />Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado mi: “Nekke kọọk iwuod baña mme usʌñ mfo. <verse eid="HAG 1:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HAG 1:8" />Dọọk kaa ke anyọñ ikpọabod nyʌñ ke ben eto dibọp ufọk mmi, nọ ami mbọ inemesịd ke anye ñnyʌñ mbọ ukpono,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> abo. <verse eid="HAG 1:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HAG 1:9" />“Ndufo emaedot anyen ke uwak, ado anye amaakappa ado etək-etək. Se ekeben enyọñ ufọk, ami mmaafuut nduọọk. Ntak-a?” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atommo. “Ke ntak ufọk mmi, a-abaaha ke ñwuudo, ke ini afịd ndufo etịmmeke esịn ifịk ke adibọp ufọk ndufo. <verse eid="HAG 1:9" /><verse number="10" style="v" sid="HAG 1:10" />Ke ntoro, ke ntak ndufo mme anyọñ emʌm ntuhube ammọ ekama, isọñ ñko amʌm mme mfịd amọ. <verse eid="HAG 1:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HAG 1:11" />Ami mmaakoot nsaad isọñ nsịn ke inwañ ye ke abod, ke mme abakpa, mme ufa ukọd, adan ọlif ye afịd ñkpọ se isọñ anwịm, ke mme awo ye ke mme ufene, ye ke afịd ubọkutom ndufo.”<verse eid="HAG 1:11" /></para>
  <para style="b" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="HAG 1:12" />Ndin Serubabel ayịn Sieltiel, Yọsua ayịn Yosadak, akwa aku, ye afịd mme ñyọhọnsʌhọ awo emaekpono uyio <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ ye etob prọfed Hakai, sia <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Abasi ammọ akedọñ anye. Ñko mme awo emaebaak <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>.<verse eid="HAG 1:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HAG 1:13" />Ndin Hakai, isʌñutom <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>, amaanọ mme awo etob <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> ami: “Ami mmọdo mba ye ndufo,” <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. <verse eid="HAG 1:13" /><verse number="14" style="v" sid="HAG 1:14" />Ndin <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaabəkko sịbidịd Serubabel ayịn Sieltiel, adaukara ke Yuda, ye sịbidịd Yọsua ayịn Yosadak, akwa aku, ye sịbidịd afịd mme ñyọhọnsʌhọ awo. Ammọ emaedi enyʌñ etọọñọ adinam utom ke ufọk <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan, Abasi ammọ, <verse eid="HAG 1:14" /><verse number="15" style="v" sid="HAG 1:15" />ke ayọhọ usen edịb mme inaañ ke ayọhọ afiọñ itiokeed.</para>
  <para style="s1" vid="HAG 1:15">Enwọñọ Ubọọñ Ufa Ufọk</para>
  <para style="p" vid="HAG 1:15">Ke ayọhọ isua iba a-Adidem Dariọs akedaaha ukara,<verse eid="HAG 1:15" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HAG 1" />
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="HAG 2" />
  <para style="nb">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="HAG 2:1" />ke ayọhọ usen edịb mme keed ke ayọhọ afiọñ itiaba, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaato prọfed Hakai adi: <verse eid="HAG 2:1" /><verse number="2" style="v" sid="HAG 2:2" />“Tañ nọ Serubabel ayịn Sieltiel, adaiwuod ukara ke Yuda, nọ Yọsua ayịn Yosadak, akwa aku, ñko ye afịd mme ñyọhọnsʌhọ awo. Bịp ammọ, <verse eid="HAG 2:2" /><verse number="3" style="v" sid="HAG 2:3" />‘Anie awo ke atu ndufo se isʌhọ akekịt ufọk ami ke akaan ubọọñ amọ? Idahami anye abadie? Nte anye ibaaha ndufo nte ikpu-ikpu ñkpọ? <verse eid="HAG 2:3" /><verse number="4" style="v" sid="HAG 2:4" />Ado idahami, sọñ idem Serubabel,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. ‘Sọñ idem, Yọsua ayịn Yosadak, akwa aku. Isọñ idem, afịd ndufo mbon isọñ,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ, ‘inyʌñ inam utom. Sia ami mmọdo mba ye ndufo,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. <verse eid="HAG 2:4" /><verse number="5" style="v" sid="HAG 2:5" />‘Ami ado se ami ñkenwọñọ ye ndufo idaha a-ndufo ekewuọñọke ke Iyib. Ñko sịbidịd mmi mmọdo aba ye ndufo. Ikiikop ndịk.’<verse eid="HAG 2:5" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="HAG 2:6" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado ami: ‘Ke etək-etək ini ami ñyaamaana ñnyeeñe mme hefịn ye isọñ, akpainyañ ye nsaad isọñ. <verse eid="HAG 2:6" /><verse number="7" style="v" sid="HAG 2:7" />Ami ñyaanyeeñe afịd mme idịd, ndin se ido udọñ afịd mme idịd ayaadi, ndin ami ñyaayọhọ ufọk ami ye ubọọñ,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. <verse eid="HAG 2:7" /><verse number="8" style="v" sid="HAG 2:8" />‘Silfa ado ake mmi kold ñko ado ake mi,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. <verse eid="HAG 2:8" /><verse number="9" style="v" sid="HAG 2:9" />‘Ubọọñ ufọk anye ami ayaakpon akan ubọọñ akaan ufọk,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ. ‘Ñko ke itie ami ñyaanọ emem,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.”<verse eid="HAG 2:9" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Adidiọñ Mbon e-Esappake</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="HAG 2:10" />Ke ayọhọ usen edịb mme inaañ ke ayọhọ afiọñ usʌkkeed, ke ayọhọ isua iba a-Adidem Dariọs akedaaha ukara, ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadi abịne prọfed Hakai: <verse eid="HAG 2:10" /><verse number="11" style="v" sid="HAG 2:11" />“Se <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ado ami: ‘Ibịp mme aku se mbed atañ: <verse eid="HAG 2:11" /><verse number="12" style="v" sid="HAG 2:12" />Adieke awo abenne unam e-emaekediọñ ke ñyeriye afọñ amọ, ndin ñyeriye afọñ ado atuuk usʌk uyo me abak, me ukọd, adan ọlif me ndidia mfen, nte anye asʌk ado se emaekediọñ?’ ”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="HAG 2:12">Mme aku emaebọọrọ, “Iyoo.”<verse eid="HAG 2:12" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="HAG 2:13" />Ndin Hakai amaabo, “Adieke awo asappake idem amọ ato adituuk akpo adituuhọ keed ke atu mme ñkpọ ami, nte esappa anye?”</para>
  <para style="p" vid="HAG 2:13">Mme aku ebọọrọ, “Ii, e-esappa.”<verse eid="HAG 2:13" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="HAG 2:14" />Ndin Hakai amaabo, “ ‘Naña aba adom ye mbon ami ye mme idịd ami ke iso mmi,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. ‘Se adodo a-ammọ ekpenamma, ye se adodo a-ammọ ekpenọọhọ ke itie ado e-ekappa se emaesappa.<verse eid="HAG 2:14" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="HAG 2:15" />“ ‘Idahami nekke kọọk iwuod baña ñkpọ ami tọọñọ ke mfịn ami kaa iso, kere baña naña ñkpọ akeba mbemiso eben itiad keed edot ke anyọñ itiad mfen ke tembịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. <verse eid="HAG 2:15" /><verse number="16" style="v" sid="HAG 2:16" />Awo ndomokeed a-akediighe ebono udomo ñkpọ edịb, duob kpọd akesʌhọ. Awo ndomokeed a-akekaaha itie unịm abañ ukọd adikoi udomo ñkpọ aba mme duob, edịb kpọd akesʌhọ. <verse eid="HAG 2:16" /><verse number="17" style="v" sid="HAG 2:17" />Ami mmaawot afịd ubọkutom ndufo ye idiọọk udọñọ, ntọdibọ ye edịmitiad, ado ndufo ikitịmmeke iñkeene miin,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ. <verse eid="HAG 2:17" /><verse number="18" style="v" sid="HAG 2:18" />Tọọñọ ke usen mfịn, tọọñọ ke ayọhọ usen edịb mme inaañ ami ke afiọñ usʌkkeed, inekke ikọọk iwuod ibaña usen e-ekesịnne itiad idakisọñ ufọk tembịd <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char>. Inekke ikọọk iwuod ibaña: <verse eid="HAG 2:18" /><verse number="19" style="v" sid="HAG 2:19" />Nte mfịd ndomokeed asʌhọ ke itie unịm mfịd? Tutu awuọ idahami, mme fain ye mme eto fik, ye pomekrened ye eto ọlif inwịmme mfịd.</para>
  <para style="p" vid="HAG 2:19">“ ‘Tọọñọ ke usen mfịn, ami ñyaudiọñ fiin.’ ”<verse eid="HAG 2:19" /></para>
  <para style="s1">Serubabel, Ñkpannuun Idiọọñọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="HAG 2:20" />Ikọ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> amaadisịm Hakai ayọhọ akañ iba ke ayọhọ usen edịb mme inaañ ke afiọñ ado: <verse eid="HAG 2:20" /><verse number="21" style="v" sid="HAG 2:21" />“Dọkkọ Serubabel adaukara ke Yuda ate ke ami ñyaadinyeeñe mme hefịn ye ederimbod. <verse eid="HAG 2:21" /><verse number="22" style="v" sid="HAG 2:22" />Ami ñyaayʌt mme ebekpo ubọọñ ñkappa ñnyʌñ nsuan adudu mme abioubọọñ asen idịd. Ami ñyaasio mme sariọd ye mme andiwad nduọñọ; mme enañmbakara ye mme andiwad eyaeduọññọ keedekeed ato ke akañkañ ayịneka amọ awodeen.<verse eid="HAG 2:22" /></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" sid="HAG 2:23" />“ ‘Ke usen ado,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ ate, ‘Ami ñyauben fiin, ayịnufọk mmi Serubabel ayịn Sieltiel,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> atañ, ‘ndin ñyaunam fiin nte ñkpannuun idiọọñọ mmi, sia ami mmaumek fiin,’ <char style="nd">Abọọñ</char> Andikponñkan atañ.”<verse eid="HAG 2:23" /></para>
  <chapter eid="HAG 2" />
</usx>